          "reply": "Main finding: the clearest useful-enquiry angle is helping shoppers choose between sun protection and everyday hydration—not trying to beat every competitor on price. Mira Nile sits below one verified same-size moisturizer comparator; the sunscreen picture is mixed, and some rival prices aren’t clear enough for a fair comparison.\n\nSunscreen\nYour SPF 50 is EGP 320 for 50 ml. Cairo Drop lists Telofill SPF 50+ gel-cream, 60 ml for EGP 329, and AVUVA sunscreen cream, 120 ml for EGP 329. That’s EGP 9 more upfront; the calculated prices are EGP 6.40/ml for yours, versus EGP 5.48/ml and EGP 2.74/ml. Your sunscreen’s format is unspecified, so treat these as shelf references, not exact matches. [Telofill](https://cairodrop.com/products/telofill-sunscreen-gel-cream-spf-50-fast-absorbing-60ml) · [AVUVA](https://cairodrop.com/products/avuva-sunscreen-cream-for-daily-protection-120ml)\n\nInfinity lists SPF 50 cream and oily-skin gel, but its pages show conflicting price/discount figures and no sizes. NUT’s B5 is positioned as an SPF 50 PA++++ lotion; its page shows conflicting prices and doesn’t confirm the selected-size price. [Infinity cream](https://infinityclinicpharma.com/products/infinity-naturals-sunscreen-cream-spf-50-all-skin-types) · [Infinity gel](https://infinityclinicpharma.com/products/naturals-sun-screen-gel-spf-50-oily-skin) · [NUT B5](https://nutbotanicals.com/products/b5-skinprotect-invisible-sunscreen-lotion-spf-50-pa-broad-spectrum)\n\nDaily moisturizers\nYour moisturizer is EGP 250 for 50 ml. Cairo Drop’s Femme Naturelle is EGP 439 for 50 ml—EGP 189 more. That’s one confirmed same-size comparison, not a full market ranking. NUT emphasizes niacinamide and hyaluronic acid; its page lists multiple sizes, so EGP 185 isn’t safely tied to 50 ml. Cairo Drop’s other moisturizers span basic hydration and targeted gels, but several list grams or no size. [Femme Naturelle](https://cairodrop.com/products/femme-naturelle-moisturizing-cream-50ml) · 